<script setup lang="ts">
import { computed, nextTick, onMounted, ref, watch } from 'vue'
import renderMathInElement from 'katex/contrib/auto-render'
import { cycloneWaves } from '../../../engineering/waves/windWaves'
const windSpeed = ref(Number(localStorage.getItem('marine-calculators:cyclone-wind:v1') ?? 45)); watch(windSpeed, value => localStorage.setItem('marine-calculators:cyclone-wind:v1', String(value)))
const result = computed(() => cycloneWaves(windSpeed.value))
onMounted(async()=>{await nextTick();const el=document.querySelector('.cyclone-background');if(el)renderMathInElement(el as HTMLElement,{delimiters:[{left:'$$',right:'$$',display:true},{left:'$',right:'$',display:false}],throwOnError:false})})
</script>
<template><section class="calculator" aria-labelledby="cyclone-title"><div class="calculator-heading"><h1 id="cyclone-title">Cyclone Generated Waves (Kumar et al., 2003)</h1></div><div class="calculator-grid no-chart-grid"><article class="panel input-panel"><div class="panel-title input-title"><h2>Input</h2></div><label>Wind Speed <span>(m/s)</span><input v-model.number="windSpeed" type="number" min="0" max="100" step="1" /></label></article><article class="panel output-panel"><div class="panel-title output-title"><h2>Output</h2></div><dl class="results"><div><dt>Significant Wave Height (<i>H</i><sub>s</sub>)</dt><dd>{{ result.significantWaveHeight.toFixed(2) }} m</dd></div><div><dt>Peak Period (<i>T</i><sub>p</sub>)</dt><dd>{{ result.peakPeriod.toFixed(2) }} s</dd></div><div><dt>Atmospheric Pressure (<i>p</i><sub>a</sub>)</dt><dd>{{ result.atmosphericPressure.toFixed(0) }} mbar</dd></div></dl></article></div><article class="background-panel"><div class="background-title"><h2>Background</h2><span>−</span></div><div class="background-body cyclone-background"><p>Kumar et al. (2003) give the following simple estimates:</p><div class="equation">$$H_s=0.25U_{max},\qquad T_p=4.5H_s^{0.48}$$</div><p>These relationships were developed from 34 cyclones along the Indian coastline and are intended only as ballpark estimates. The original paper reports poorer performance for $H_s&lt;3\,\mathrm{m}$.</p><div class="equation">$$p_a=1012.6-0.6077785U_{10}-0.01079967U_{10}^2$$</div><p>The Wooten pressure regression was developed for wind speeds up to 78 m/s and pressures down to approximately 880 mbar.</p><p><strong>References</strong><br />Kumar, V. S., Mandal, S., &amp; Kumar, K. A. (2003). Estimation of wind speed and wave height during cyclones. <em>Ocean Engineering, 30</em>(17), 2239–2253.<br />Wooten, R. D. (2011). Statistical analysis of the relationship between wind speed, pressure and temperature. <em>Journal of Applied Sciences, 11</em>(15), 2712–2722.</p></div></article></section></template>
